(Plan 230 stage A4 — the consumer-side goal fixture. A pure-Vox library
exporting a two-argument function and a parameterless one, so a `see` consumer
can call `add two numbers of 3 and 4` and print 7 — the end-to-end proof that
plans 200 and 230 exist for, and the acceptance line this whole stage serves.
`greet` is exported too so the name-resolution tests can import a `greet` that
collides with a local definition (shadowing) or with another library's export
(ambiguity).

Built with `vox mathkit_lib.vox --shared -o libmathkit.so`, which writes
`libmathkit.lib` beside it; the consumer `see`s the `.lib`, never the `.so`.)

Library mathkit version "1.0".

To 'add two numbers' with a number called aa and a number called b.
  Return a number, aa add b.

To greet.
  Print "hi from mathkit".